blurb = "Depicts sightseers viewing cherry blossoms along the banks of the Tama River at Edo.

The scene is situated along the Tamagawa Aqueduct flowing south of Naito-Shinjuku, a post town on the Kōshū Kaidō road. To the right are the houses of the post town, and to the left is a row of cherry trees planted during the Kyōhō era (1716-1736) to reinforce the embankment."
